  "dct_description_sm": [
    "This dataset contains Copernicus EMS Rapid Mapping products for activation EMSR922. Starting from 14 August at 22:00 UTC a wildfire started to spread on different areas. The event is ongoing and the most serious fires are currently near Herceg Novi (Bijela and Baošići) and Ulcinj, where strong winds have helped the fires spread. Several homes were threatened, and some residents were temporarily evacuated as a precaution. Additional fires have been reported near Bar, Nikšić, Kolašin, and Cetinje. Firefighters, volunteers, military , and AFFF with planes and helicopters are actively engaged. Copernicus EMS Rapid Mapping is requested to provide burnt area delineation and damage assessment emergency mapping **Citation:** Copernicus Emergency Management Service (© 2026 European Union), EMSR922 **Product types present in this dataset's resources:** **DEL (Delineation)**: maps the extent of the event itself (eg. flood, fire, landslide boundary). **GRA (Grading)**: assesses damage to individual features (eg. buildings, infrastructure). Where a GeoPackage download is available for an Area of Interest/round, it already contains every layer with its official Copernicus styling and colours - prefer it in GIS software over the zipped shapefile download."
  ],
